  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DFAT bilateral funding to World Health Organization (WHO) Country Office PNG 2018 - 2023</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This investment supports  Australia&apos;s Department of Foreign Affairs and Trade (DFAT) - World Health Organization (WHO) Papua New Guinea (PNG) Bilateral Partnership 2018-2023. Three key outcome areas were identified for DFAT support to PNG, aimed at improving health outcomes: 1) improve prevention, detection and response to high burden communicable diseases and health security threats; 2) improve utilisation of government finance and improve health worker recruitment so that rural primary health care centres are delivering essential care including antenatal care and integrated child care; and 3) improved quality client centred, integrated HIV, reproductive health and voluntary family planning services.</narrative>
  </description>
